<title>BELGIUM: Belgium to scrap tax on listed stocks.</title>
<headline>Belgium to scrap tax on listed stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said on Tuesday it would scrap the annual tax of 0.042 percent on listed stocks to lift fiscal obstacles for new bourse listings.</p>
<p>It said the tax had inspired companies to reduce the share of listed capital, which weighed on the bourse's liquidity.</p>
<p>The measure will have a negative impact on the budget of 600 million francs, it said.</p>
